---
// Import the layout
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import droneImage from "../images/drone.jpg";
---

<Layout title="About - Frodsham Townfield Allotments">
  <!-- MAIN CONTENT SECTION -->
  <section
    class="hero"
    style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-neutral) 0%, var(--color-accent-light) 100%);"
  >
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <h2 style="color: var(--color-primary); text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);">
          About Frodsham Townfield Allotments
        </h2>
      <p>
        Advice is always forthcoming from others on the plots and even if it is
        sometimes contradictory it is always right! The inevitable gluts of
        produce are always shared so you can go home with rhubarb even if you
        don't grow it.
      </p>

      <p>
        Allotment holders get a great deal of satisfaction from their hobby and
        it’s great for exercise – so much better than paying a gym sub to
        exercise indoors with no fresh air. There is tremendous variety in the
        plots with lots of flowers, fruit trees and chickens as well as the
        traditional rows of vegetables.
      </p>

        <p>
          Even if you have never grown anything before, why not give it a try? If
          it seems a bit daunting, how about teaming up with someone to share a
          plot? Other plotholders will be happy to give advice and a bit of help
          if needed. Spare seeds, plug plants and cuttings are often on offer to
          help get started.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="text-align: center;">
        <img
          src={droneImage.src}
          alt="Frodsham Townfield Allotments aerial view"
          style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-lg);"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HISTORY SECTION -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--color-neutral); padding: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <h2 style="color: var(--color-primary); text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);">
          A Brief History of AFTA
        </h2>
      <p>
        The site opened at Easter 2011 on what had previously been a farm field.
        Initially the plots were marked out with pegs and string and from that
        daunting start has emerged the lively and colourful site that exists
        today
      </p>
      <p>
        AFTA developed from discussions between the Plot holders and Atlantic
        Hardware the landowners, to provide more local day to day management of
        the site and promote and develop it with the wider community in the
        area. As a result AFTA was established in Nov 2012 with a constitution
        and committee and initially 30 members.
      </p>
      <p>
        The main aim of the association is to be a collective voice working with
        the landowners and all our members to develop the plots and facilities
        on the site, and undertake the day to day maintenance of the field.
      </p>
      <p>
        We look after the communal compost area and cut the grass on the tracks
        and walkways. We have an association shed and a secure container by the
        car park known as the Tardis. We organise deliveries of compost and
        shredded material for paths. We liaised with the Woodland Trust to
        provide hedge trees which we have planted at the bottom end of the
        field.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our committee meetings allocate tasks to committee members and plans and
        ideas to promote, safeguard and improve the allotments. We meet four
        times a year on average. However, there is always the opportunity to
        discuss an develop new ideas
      </p>
      <p>
        The Association now has a membership of over 90 and is affiliated to the
        National Allotment Association. The site has expanded from 30 plots to
        over 80 plots, plus the Good Shed NHS plot, and a Bee apiary.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ACTIVITIES SECTION -->
  <section style="background-color: #ffffff; padding: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="color: var(--color-primary); text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);">
        Things We Do
      </h2>
      <div
        style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: var(--spacing-lg);"
      >
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">
            Raising the profile of the allotments locally by publicity and
            adverts
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">
            Contact with and working with other groups locally and in related
            areas like the garden club and the Town council allotments
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">
            Building contacts with local and County Council, Community Police,
            Frodsham Transition Initiative and members of the local community.
            Local councillors and the MP have all been on site visits to see
            what has been achieved at the site
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">Stall at the Frodsham Community event</p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">
            Exploring collaborative events and funding opportunities, contact
            with other local allotment associations (Kingsley)
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">Site visits from the NW region of the National Association</p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">
            We are working on plans to improve composting facilities at the site
          </p>
        </div>
        <div
          class="card"
          style="border: 2px solid var(--color-border); border-top: 4px solid var(--color-accent); background: white; padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);"
        >
          <p style="color: var(--color-text); margin: 0; line-height: 1.7;">
            We have a fully serviced portaloo on site for plot holders to use
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .container {
      max-width: 1200px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--spacing-lg);
    }

    .card {
      transition: var(--transition);
    }

    .card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .container {
        padding: 0 var(--spacing-md);
      }

      h2 {
        font-size: 1.75rem;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .container {
        padding: 0 var(--spacing-sm);
      }

      div[style*="display: flex"] {
        flex-direction: column !important;
      }

      div[style*="display: flex"] a {
        width: 100% !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>